# {{app_name}}: CI/CD and release setup

The workflows in `.github/workflows/` and the lanes in `ios/fastlane/` were
generated by flutter-kickstart. They need these one-time, human steps before
the build-and-deploy workflows can succeed. `pr_checks.yml` works
immediately.

Application ids (read from the native projects at scaffold time):

| Flavor | Android | iOS |
| --- | --- | --- |
| development | `{{android_id}}.dev` | `{{ios_id}}.dev` |
| staging | `{{android_id}}.stg` | `{{ios_id}}.stg` |
| production | `{{android_id}}` | `{{ios_id}}` |

## 1. GitHub Actions secrets

Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions. Skip the iOS rows if the app
doesn't target iOS.

| Secret | Used for |
| --- | --- |
| `API_BASE_URL` | Optional. Overrides the per-flavor default in `lib/main_<flavor>.dart` (use GitHub *environments* for one value per flavor) |
| `ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64` | Upload keystore: `base64 -i upload.jks \| pbcopy` |
| `ANDROID_KEYSTORE_ALIAS`, `ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD`, `ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD` | Read by `android/app/build.gradle.kts` |
| `PLAY_STORE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON` | Play Console upload (production) |
| `FIREBASE_APP_ID_ANDROID`, `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT` | Firebase App Distribution (development/staging) |
| `APP_STORE_CONNECT_API_KEY_ID`, `APP_STORE_CONNECT_API_ISSUER_ID`, `APP_STORE_CONNECT_API_KEY_CONTENT` | Fastlane auth to App Store Connect |
| `IOS_CERTIFICATE_BASE64`, `IOS_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD` | Distribution certificate (`.p12`, base64) |
| `IOS_PROVISIONING_PROFILE_BASE64` | App Store provisioning profile (base64) |
| `KEYCHAIN_PASSWORD` | Any random string for the temporary CI keychain |
{{crash_secrets}}

## 2. Android signing

Already wired: `android/app/build.gradle.kts` reads the `ANDROID_KEYSTORE_*`
variables in CI, or `android/key.properties` locally:

```properties
storeFile=/absolute/path/to/upload.jks
storePassword=...
keyAlias=upload
keyPassword=...
```

`key.properties` and `*.jks` are already in `.gitignore`. Create a keystore
with:

```bash
keytool -genkey -v -keystore upload.jks -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 -alias upload
```

## 3. iOS signing

`ios/fastlane/Fastfile` imports the certificate and profile from the
secrets above. If the team uses `match`, replace its `before_all` block
with `match(type: "appstore", readonly: true)`. Set the Apple team in Xcode
(Runner target -> Signing & Capabilities) for every configuration.

